Candidates' names will not be made public.
Trump himself wouldn't mind if he got the Nobel Prize.
In May, a reporter asked him at the White House if he thought he deserved the Peace Prize.
That's what everyone thinks, but I'd never say it myself," Trump said with a smile.
I want to get this done.
“The prize I want is a victory for the whole world,” the president continued, referring to the North Korea talks.
However, there are things that make Trumb's Nobel Nobel improbable.
The Norwegian Nobel Committee, which concludes the prize, has often given recognition to individuals and organizations representing liberal democracy and the multifaceted world order - exactly the kind of international cooperation that Trump has seen as his opponent.
In the 21st century, there have been three U.S
Rewarding Trump would therefore require an ideological turnaround from the Nobel Committee.
Fire notification in the tunnel: Motorists behaved like lemmings and drove in the wrong direction
Traffic chaos that took place on Ykköstie in Lohja took place on 8 September.
Due to the advertisement, traffic in the tunnel area was interrupted in the direction of both Turku and Helsinki.
When it became clear that this was a system failure, the fire department tried to make the traffic normal.
However, it did not succeed very quickly.
We tried to open the road once before, but the Road Traffic Centre said that it cannot be opened, because there are motorists on the road and they are driving whatever happens, the on-call fire chief Pasi Kääriäinen told STT at the time.
At that time, we even started driving in the wrong direction just a moment after waiting.
When the first one starts to act against the traffic rules, a few others are often followed, says Tapio Heiskanen, Traffic Safety's Liaison Manager.
According to traffic rules, motorways and tunnels should only stop for a compelling reason.
Liikenneturva reminds that in exceptional situations it is not possible to start endangering traffic with hasty solutions.
Alarm vehicles shall always be provided as unobstructed as possible.
Driving in the opposite direction on the motorway is especially forbidden, as well as making and reversing a u-turn.
The same prohibitions also apply in tunnels, where you always have to turn on the headlights.
Stopping without a compelling reason is also forbidden, as is parking, of course.
Recently, there have even been cases where the driver has stopped in the tunnel to brush the snow from his car.
It should be clear that this is the wrong place and time for the activities in question," Heiskanen says in a traffic safety press release.
Ilves fans would have wanted to continue their party, even though the ship got caught on the bottom of the lake
The Ilves fans transported by the inland ship M/S Tampere would have wanted to stay on the ship to continue their victory celebrations, even though the ship had been caught on the bottom of the lake, says Juho Syrjä, who was the ship's commander at the time of the incident.
M/S Tampere, who was on his way from Hämeenlinna to Tampere, drifted off his route late Saturday evening and got caught at the bottom of the bow in Vanajavesi, Akaa.
19 passengers and five crew were evacuated to the mainland at night.
No one was injured.
Ilves fans would have wanted to continue their party on the ship until the morning, but of course it made more sense to send them to the harbor with the fire department and by bus home, Syrjä told STT.
Ilves fans had been in Hämeenlinna to watch Ilves and HPK's match, which ended with Ilves' 4-3 victory.
According to Syrjä, Saturday's accident was due to the fact that the surface of the water in Vanajavesi was about half a meter lower than normal.
According to Syrjä, the navigation was also hampered by the fact that the nearest fairway badge was covered with gulls, which is why its reflectors were not normally visible in the dark autumn bridge.
No more noticeable collision
Haveri took place on the western side of Jumusensalmi shortly since the ferry route had swerved the highway bridge between Tampere and Helsinki.
According to Syrjä, there was no greater dramatic drama involved in the incident, as the speed of the vessel was very low at the time of the incident, and hitting the bottom did not cause a more noticeable collision.
According to Syrjä, getting caught at the bottom has not caused any leaks or depressions on the ship, and it is expected that the ship's cruises will continue as normal.
The diver went on Saturday morning to check the condition of the ship before the ship was towed off from the shallows.
As a precaution, we will go to the shipyard to check that there was no damage, Syrjä says.
Syrjä believes that M/S Tampere's next cruise booked for next weekend can be taken care of as agreed.
According to him, the cruise season will continue until Independence Day.
No use for ambulances
Emergency services were alerted on Saturday night just after midnight.
Ambulances were alerted to Viiala port to receive evacuated passengers, but there was no use for ambulances.
On-call Fire Chief Matti Willman told late in the evening that the evacuation conditions on the lake were difficult due to the darkness and the rather strong breeze.
The Pirkanmaa Rescue Department announced after half past three o'clock on Sunday that everyone on board had been evacuated and the passengers have been transferred by bus to Tampere.
Built in 1957, the cruiser was restored in 2001, 2014 and 2017.
Trump's refereeing nominee accused of harassing and drinking may be left without a top-of-the-top position
Brett Kavanaugh, who has been presented as a U.S. Supreme Court justice, may well be left without the position he has sought, says Programme Director Mika Aaltola from the Finnish Institute of International Affairs.
To date, at least three women have accused Kavanaugh of sexual assault and inappropriate behavior during their studies.
According to Aaltola, doubts have put so much political pressure on the Republican Party that President Donald Trump may end up pretending to be someone else.
From time to time in the United States, it has occasionally occurred that the president's nominee for a Supreme Court of Justice has aroused many contradictions.
In this case, the referee nominee has usually withdrawn himself, says Aaltola.
In this way, the president has been able to maintain his face.
It's going to get the nomination to the Democrats
The U.S. Supreme Court strives to be above politics, but at least in Kavanaugh's case, the election of a new judge has become a politically very sensitive process.
If Kavanaugh is appointed, according to Aaltola, the decision is likely to rain down on the Democratic Party in the upcoming congressory elections.
It would increase the enthusiasm to vote among young people and women who would be more likely to vote for Democrats.
On the other hand, the appointment of a conservative judge to the Supreme Court would be a long-standing victory for Republicans.
The appointment will not take place for every presidential term, as in the United States, Supreme Court judges will be appointed for a lifetime.
In practice, some of them have retired at the age of about 70 to 80.
Some Republicans have doubts about the nomination
The U.S. Supreme Court's judicial nominees are normally subjected to a background check, Aaltola says.
Even though Trump has only set a deadline of a week for the FBI's further investigation, according to Aaltola, it can still bring up something relevant.
Yeah, it might bring.
Rarely there is smoke without fire, says Aaltola.
According to Aaltola, it is at least certain that Kavanaugh's suitability or inappropriatity for the position will be discussed lively before the Senate decides.
Republicans have a 51-49 majority in the Senate, but at least two female Republican senators are expected to be skeptical of Kavanaugh's appointment.
The most embarrassing thing would be that the nomination would be put to the vote and Republicans would lose.
