There would be a lot of visitors watching the drone operations of the Finnish police.
We are asked for trainings.
Is becoming even more common
Himberg reminds that it is very important to find what has disappeared in Finland's wintry conditions as soon as possible.
As has been said, in Raahe's case, the lost person was found with the help of a drone in just a few minutes.
The Finnish police have already trained hundreds of drone pilots.
According to Himberg, they are expected to be further educated.
The drone is already widely used for police duties, and their use will become more common and increasing in the future.
That's what I'd dare to say," Himberg said.
