Europe's leading stars were Tommy Fleetwood and Francesco Molinari, who won all four matches on Friday and Saturday.
In the past, no European couple had achieved this.
On Sunday, the duo will strive for more history.
No European player has won five points together in the Ryder Cup, and the Americans have only been able to score three players: Arnold Palmer and Gardiner Dickinson (1969) and Larry Nelson (1979).
HJK condemns the fierce harassment of its supporters in the Honka match: "Violence does not belong in football"
HJK released a statement on Sunday condemning the disruptive behaviour of its supporters at Saturday's FC Honka match in Tapiola.
"We regret the events after the Honka-HJK match on behalf of our supporters," the statement said.
At the end of the match, about 50 HJK supporters rushed onto the pitch and some seemed to be trying to pick a dispute with Honka's supporters.
There was also a fight between supporters.
The organizers did not calm down the situation, but police officers and horse police were also needed.
HJK says in a statement that the team's players and officials are shocked by what happened.
Post-match events are not in line with the values of our traditional 111-year-old club.
"We sharply resign ourselves from all activities that jeopardize the safety of match events," the statement said.
HJK promises to help the authorities and event organisers to investigate factors that pose a threat to safety and to eliminate side effects.
The supporter culture is part of football and an important issue for HJK.
In every way, we support positive, cheerful and encouraging activities in football grandstands.
"Violence doesn't belong to it," the statement said.
The Filipino inventor flows a drone car to avoid traffic jams
Mendiola is a Filipino inventor, hip-hop dancer and some kind of Pelle Peloton.
He's now part of a world-grooming group that swore he'd invented a flying car, or at least his own version of it.
As competitors, he has, for example, factors such as Audi and Airbus.
