I hope the device provokes positive reactions.
“This was just a dream five years ago,” Mendiola said.
JHL anticipates: Tomorrow's industrial action will be visible in children's day care and social and health services
In the public and welfare sectors, the bans on overtime and shift changes starting tomorrow are particularly visible in social and health services and in children's day care," says Päivi Niemi-Laine, Chairman of JHL.
The effects will be extensive, and they will certainly be visible in such a way that there will not be enough staff on site.
Everyone has to think about how to pick up their children.
The employer's task now is to make sure that the services work and that no one's life is threatened," Niemi-Laine told STT.
According to Niemi-Laine, the lack of employees was also visible at the beginning of the year, when JHL's members were banned from overtime and shift changes due to contract negotiations.
Employers have made it possible, through flexibility, that the staff have not been hired, but that the employees have been left overtime or changed shifts.
This is not yet an industrial action.
In terms of occupational safety and health, it is a normal thing to take care of regular working hours for each employee and only do them.
JHL opposes the Government's intention to reduce the protection against dismissal of small companies.
Markku Jalonen, Labour Market Director for Municipal Employers, will not begin to anticipate the effects of bans on overtime and shift changes.
However, he doesn't think they're very revolutionary, even though the services may deteriorate.
Employers all over Finland are aware of this and have made the preparations that can be done.
The area is so impossibly extensive, social and health services and the technical sector that it is difficult to say.
The impacts can vary very much by industry, region and employers," Jalonen told STT.
Jalonen says that last week we already had experiences of, among other things, the similar three-day activities of the Union of Practical Nurses and Primary Nurses Super and the Trade Union for Social and Health Care Tehy, which lasted three days.
Their effects were quite limited.
JHL's ban on overtime and shift changes applies, for example, to employees of municipalities, the church, the state and the private social and health care sector.
Childminders, for example, are excluded.
At this stage, the industrial action concerns almost 100 000 JHL members.
According to Niemi-Laine, JHL's actions may take a long time.
The union is also prepared for other industrial action if the preparation of the Termination Act continues.
The government should now admit that here we run to the wall and hard.
According to Jalonen, both the trade union movement and the government have to meet.
What's special about this is that the hard ones are already in the barrel, even though the presentation hasn't been given yet, Jalonen updates.
The Great Coral Reef is created by children and adults - in the fitness circles of the performance, the gestures of rays and seahorses are studied
The Great Coral Reef of the Collective in Other Premises premiered last spring in Hamburg and last Saturday it was performed for the second time in Finland, this time in Kanneltalo.
Like the group's previous works, the Great Coral Reef is a work that is built from start to finish together with the audience.
This time, however, a clearer-limited presentation will also be built, which refreshes and crystallizes the observations made in the initial exercises.
There is also fairy-tale magic for child attendees.
The child's perspective has already been included in the preparatory phase.
However, the Great Coral Reef is not a children's performance, but a performance made jointly by adults and children.
It provides adults with information and observations about children's way of receiving information and making art.
Children's ability to engage in exercises and joint play also dissolves the distance between adults and children.
The Great Coral Reef is somewhat reminiscent of fairytale ballet, the fitness circuit and nature-themed information, but for good it tunes around visits in different, non-humane conditions.
The Great Coral Reef begins with exploring the movement paths of corals and organisms and fish living on the coral reef.
In six different fitness circles, you will learn, among other things, the gestures of rays and seahorses.
Finally, a performance of less than an hour will be made, in which music, lights and shiny paints and costumes will help to get to know the life of the coral reef.
In the Great Coral Reef, there are both diving people who observe the life of the coral reef, as well as the corals to look at.
In addition, there are organisms that look at corals.
In many directions, the gazes and observations made the performance dense and bustling with life.
Whether it's the landscape of an organism, an organism looking at the landscape, and another organism or landscape looking at an organism - and all this at the same time.
It doesn't seem difficult for children.
With its exercises, the group strives for the boundary between thinking and activities, which can be reached when a group consists of both children and adults is challenging.
On the other hand, the involvement of children makes it more important.
After the workshop, a silent demonstration on behalf of endangered corals will be held at Sitrator.
Destructions that go beyond man's comprehension should not be allowed to harden, although it could be difficult to comprehend the importance of practicing one's own sympathy in the face of vision of destruction.
In other spaces, it has built its work in such a way that it respects the diversity of life also with a political gesture.
There are other generations, there are different kinds of consciousnesses, other species and their future generations, for whose wonder and play it clears space.
The kids grow up too fast - I'm happy there weren't any smartphones in my childhood
Today's children and young people are increasingly irresponsible.
Young people start smoking and drinking all the time when they are younger and younger.
In my opinion, children should be children throughout their childhood and not mess with their lives for the sake of intoxicants and sex, because others say they do.
I was overwhelmed when a friend of mine told me that he had had to pick up his fifth-grade sister from a "boyfriend" on the weekend.
When she came to pick up her intoxicated sister, she told me about her sexual experiences that night.
I couldn't possibly imagine my own sister in the same situation, because we've been told and warned throughout our childhood that intoxicants shouldn't be touched and sex is an adult thing.
I hope that today's children will be able to live a proper childhood, and they wouldn't have to grow up too early due to the group pressure created by their friends.
I'm constantly seeing more and more younger girls on Instagram, who are wearing make-up in their photos and revealing their clothes.
Snapchat is used in the evenings to take and send revealing photos.
It's even more difficult to guess how old the girls are.
Today's 13-year-olds can easily look like 18-year-olds and parents.
My childhood consisted of playing in the woods and playing board games.
I'm glad I didn't have smartphones in my childhood.
I got to be a child for many years and didn't have to think about what others think of me.
Authorities have told the state leadership that the incident is not related to national security
According to Ilkka Kanerva interviewed by Yle, the Security Police and the Finnish Defence Forces went to inform the Defence and Foreign Affairs Committees earlier this week.
Finland's state leadership has been told that Airiston Helmi's investigation is currently not related to national security, but to organised crime, Yle reported.
Ilkka Kanerva (National Coalition Party), Chairman of the Defence Committee (National Coalition Party), confirmed the information of the sources that appeared anonymously.
According to Kanerva, the Defence Forces and the Security Police went to the Defence and Foreign Affairs Committees this week to report on the ongoing investigation.
This is primarily considered financial crime.
They were quite strict that they didn't speculate that there would be something else," Kanerva commented in an interview with Yle.
According to Yle's information, no evidence of national security has been found about the seized material so far, but the investigation is only just beginning.
We cannot yet know what may be revealed from it, says one of Yle's interviewees.
Extensive home searches, which began a week ago in the Turku archipelago and on the mainland, have raised the question of whether the investigation is mere economic crime or a threat to Finland's internal security.
Earlier this week, Iltalehti compiled an article discussing the allegations both for and against.
