7 x the most beautiful luminaire - here you will recognize a good lamp
Awaken the space to life, create the right atmosphere in the decor and read the book without tiring eyes.
It's worth investing in good lighting.
We gathered together three good reasons to invest in lighting.
The tips were given by Tarja Jokiniemi, Sales and Marketing Director at Innolux.
Done a favor for your eyes
The importance of illumination is increasing, the more ages there are.
Sufficient light can be used to help with problems that come with age, as vision accuracy decreases and more and more people suffer from glare.
As we get older, the need for light also increases.
People in their sixties need three times more light than a twenty-year-old.
Therefore, it is worth investing in the caring effects of light and the features of the luminaire already for health reasons.
A good luminaire gives enough light, but not dazzling, Jokiniemi hints.
Creates beauty around you
The beautiful interior can only be displayed with the right lighting solutions.
Today's decorator can afford to choose.
The Japanese style, which combines Scandinavianism and Japaneseness, is unfamiliar.
On the other hand, the modern and playful retro style inspired by the 70's with its strong colors, different shades of metal or ice cream colors has also become a boom.
Genuiness fascinates in the same way as the rest of the home's interior.
The materials now show wood, concrete, ceramics, paper, leather and bamboo.
Embody your personality
On the other hand, we are now investing more in the home than before, and the interior has become a way of expressing itself.
Instead of mass production, we want a tailor-made, even a bold lamp for our own home, which has a story to tell.
People are clearly looking for Finnish and Nordic products, the origin and designer of which are known.
So let's be very design-conscious," Jokiniemi says.
You don't necessarily buy the latest trend lamp for your home, but a timeless classic, for which many years have been saved.
Certain kinds of timeless, jewelry-like and elegant classics hold their own year after year, Jokiniemi says.
Thank you and goodbye!
