The player wants to set an example in recycling - the goods are sent to the world in recycling boxes, the plastic switched to paper
In addition to the games, Pelimies, a specialty of games, now also recycles packaging materials.
Brick-and-mortar store customers' products are no longer packaged in plastic bags, but in paper bags made of recycled material.
Products ordered from the online store are packaged, for example, in packages from importers.
Anyone of the packages that come to us will be reused.
We may use the drawers a dozen times, as long as the package is in such condition that it can be used, Ville Puurula from Oulun Pelimies says.
As padding material, the company mainly uses newspapers and other similar recycled materials.
Bubble plastic is avoided as far as possible.
In the near future, we intend to switch to recycled material even in envelopes.
The movement wants to set an example for others.
According to Puurula, recycling does not cause any extra inconvenience.
It's not a big problem to start recycling.
It also generates financial savings when, for example, cardboard packaging is reused.
Recycling is a natural fit for Pelimies' operations, as in addition to new products, the store's central product range includes, among other things, used games and equipment.
Acquisition of everyone who is fashion-conscious: One and the same shirt works in every outfit
